# armour/woman/lamellar: lamellar cut to the woman (ARMOUR-W, wave 2; STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.4, 14 and 29.6): the
# man's laced lame rows (armour/man/lamellar) on HER plate's cut: the waist a pixel in, the shoulder caps under the
# pauldrons, and her one step-1 chest row is the first lame row's dark underside (the bust shaped by shading only). One
# lacing cord under the gorget (accent), the chest lames three rows tall (a lit top with its step-4 glint, a mid row, a
# dark underside with black lacing gaps), her belt, plain lacquer lames under it, a solid hem band. Before this map her
# lamellar fell back to the mail hauberk, so a Steppe or Jade woman lost the form and A3's brass body.
# `brassbody` views (D58, A3): the cord in metal too, so the compositor paints the whole coat in the alloy's brass (the
# people's blue stays on the collar, the cuffs and the sash). `sheen-dark,alloyshape` views: the antique sheen's lames.
# Finish regions: R the gorget's rim and the hem band, P the lit chest, G the chest socket, W a 2x2 spot on the shadow side.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L. Written by ARMOUR-W tools/mk_torso.py from src/torso_masters.txt.
use person
body woman
role armour lamellar
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

